Measured (read-only): 0.5-3.6 s pass in ForwardShowErrorMessage before the dialog reaches the page -- W906_AlarmStopLikeGolden
(stop every motor) -> W906_ShowErrorMessageRecordLikeGolden (MyDBIEvent / handler log / ProductionLog / ErrShowToForm) ->
W906_NoteAuthArm -> DialogMailboxPostAlarm (the HMI reads the mailbox every 100 ms). The mailbox post cannot simply move to the
top: W906_NoteAuthArm reads W906_ShowErrorMessage_Recorded, and the stop must stay first. So first measure: T0 entry, T1 after
the stop, T2 after the record, printed with the post as one op-log line "ALARMTIME <code> stop N ms, record N ms, auth+post N ms,
total N ms" (+ stdout). Its own line: the "query qid=" line is parsed by tools/webprobe. Behaviour unchanged.
tools/wb_serve.cpp: same lines (:440 also declares the anonymous-namespace OpLine; the printf replaces a blank line).
NoticeAck, D026_NoteAuth passed; Debug and release wb_serve linked. Backup D:\HT9045\_review\wb_serve.cpp.bak_alarmtime_20261007_180626.
WORKLOG row 173.

